Id: lin002i
Severity: WARN, INFO
Category: network
Check: check_listeningprocs
Fix: Bind each service to the address it serves, and stop the ones not needed.
References: ss(8)
Controls: CIS 4.8; NIST CM-7; ISO 8.20; CE Secure configuration

Installed processes listening on Internet interfaces must be
tightly controlled since they are the "open doors" to the
outside.

A process with sockets on ports in the kernel's ephemeral range
(/proc/sys/net/ipv4/ip_local_port_range, usually 32768-60999) is reported
once for each protocol and address as "listening on ephemeral ports",
with the ports themselves in the detail. Those ports are usually chosen
by the kernel and change from run to run, so naming them in the message
would make the finding look new every time.

IPv4 and IPv6 sockets are both reported. A process listening on 0.0.0.0
and on :: (or on one dual-stack socket) is one finding "on every
interface"; ::1 counts as loopback, like 127.0.0.0/8. A socket bound to
one device (SO_BINDTODEVICE, as DHCP clients do) is reported on that
interface. The sockets are read with ss, or lsof or netstat where ss is
missing.
